(5993735, 876121, 40391, '<td valign="top">Great shot of Sydney and timely for Anzac Day.  I feel it was left exposed for a little too long, the focus is not quite right and it would have been better to set up to remove the foreground structure (if possible). 6.</td>', 'Great shot of Sydney and timely for Anzac Day.  I feel it was left exposed for a little too long, the focus is not quite right and it would have been better to set up to remove the foreground structure (if possible). 6.', '2010-05-06 03:58:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993748, 875837, 40391, '<td valign="top">Nice location but I think you''ve tried too hard to get the moon and sacrificed the overall picture as far as lighting and exposure.  I do like the movement of the reeds in the foreground. That windmill looks fascinating and I wonder if a tighter shot with that being more prominent would have improved this shot. 5.</td>', 'Nice location but I think you''ve tried too hard to get the moon and sacrificed the overall picture as far as lighting and exposure.  I do like the movement of the reeds in the foreground. That windmill looks fascinating and I wonder if a tighter shot with that being more prominent would have improved this shot. 5.', '2010-05-06 04:04:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993755, 875841, 40391, '<td valign="top">Fell? I don''t think it''s been shot yet. Interesting shot but the pp doesn''t quite work for me. It still got my attention! 6.</td>', 'Fell? I don''t think it''s been shot yet. Interesting shot but the pp doesn''t quite work for me. It still got my attention! 6.', '2010-05-06 04:06:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993760, 876024, 40391, '<td valign="top">If you were puposefully setting this shot up the background has let you down.  I''m guessing this was an opertunistic photo which has good focus and lighting but is missing that little something for the best of the month shot. 5.  (that said I''m sure this will probably beat mine so what do I know ;-) )</td>', 'If you were puposefully setting this shot up the background has let you down.  I''m guessing this was an opertunistic photo which has good focus and lighting but is missing that little something for the best of the month shot. 5.  (that said I''m sure this will probably beat mine so what do I know ;-) )', '2010-05-06 04:10:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993764, 876009, 40391, '<td valign="top">I take it from you title that this is a natural phenomenon. I wouldn''t say this is a great photo but you have definately capture something interesting there. Overall, there is no great impact of colour and I would have liked to have seen sharper focus on the trees but overall an interesting shot. 5</td>', 'I take it from you title that this is a natural phenomenon. I wouldn''t say this is a great photo but you have definately capture something interesting there. Overall, there is no great impact of colour and I would have liked to have seen sharper focus on the trees but overall an interesting shot. 5', '2010-05-06 04:16:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993766, 876057, 40391, '<td valign="top">Loosing most of the terrestrial foreground would have improved you lovely shot. 5</td>', 'Loosing most of the terrestrial foreground would have improved you lovely shot. 5', '2010-05-06 04:19:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993768, 871046, 40391, '<td valign="top">Great lighting! 7</td>', 'Great lighting! 7', '2010-05-06 04:19:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993769, 871973, 40391, '<td valign="top">As they say - focus on the eye.  Love the colours and capture of movement. 7</td>', 'As they say - focus on the eye.  Love the colours and capture of movement. 7', '2010-05-06 04:20:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993774, 875833, 40391, '<td valign="top">Very good DoF and set up.  The B&amp;W may not have been the best choice IMHO. 5</td>', 'Very good DoF and set up.  The B&W may not have been the best choice IMHO. 5', '2010-05-06 04:24:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993811, 876004, 35545, '<td valign="top">Love the colored dresses.  Not that crazy about the girls with their mouths wide open though, but that''s just me.  Nice, clear shot.</td>', 'Love the colored dresses.  Not that crazy about the girls with their mouths wide open though, but that''s just me.  Nice, clear shot.', '2010-05-06 04:53:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993813, 875565, 35545, '<td valign="top">Great detail and textures.</td>', 'Great detail and textures.', '2010-05-06 04:53:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993816, 875954, 35545, '<td valign="top">Neat composition.  I really like the plant pots by the doors -- the only individualistic touches in the shot.</td>', 'Neat composition.  I really like the plant pots by the doors -- the only individualistic touches in the shot.', '2010-05-06 04:54:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993821, 875917, 35545, '<td valign="top">Interesting composition with the leading line of the bridge rail over to the right.  Lots of good details.  I''d like to see more of the detail, but the black border is taking up a lot of the pixels.  8(</td>', 'Interesting composition with the leading line of the bridge rail over to the right.  Lots of good details.  I''d like to see more of the detail, but the black border is taking up a lot of the pixels.  8(', '2010-05-06 04:57:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993823, 866800, 35545, '<td valign="top">Reminiscent of Georgia O''Keefe.</td>', 'Reminiscent of Georgia O''Keefe.', '2010-05-06 04:59:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993830, 875838, 35545, '<td valign="top">Neat star trails.</td>', 'Neat star trails.', '2010-05-06 05:01:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993837, 873669, 35545, '<td valign="top">Good composition.</td>', 'Good composition.', '2010-05-06 05:05:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993838, 876072, 35545, '<td valign="top">I really like the swooping lines.</td>', 'I really like the swooping lines.', '2010-05-06 05:06:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993843, 875974, 35545, '<td valign="top">Nice bokeh and composition.  Maybe a little more contrast?</td>', 'Nice bokeh and composition.  Maybe a little more contrast?', '2010-05-06 05:07:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993846, 875666, 35545, '<td valign="top">Great detail in the feathers.</td>', 'Great detail in the feathers.', '2010-05-06 05:08:11.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(5993848, 875718, 35545, '<td valign="top">Sorry.  I''m just not that crazy about dirty feet.</td>', 'Sorry.  I''m just not that crazy about dirty feet.', '2010-05-06 05:09:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993866, 872000, 35545, '<td valign="top">Very powerful feeling of movement.</td>', 'Very powerful feeling of movement.', '2010-05-06 05:15:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993894, 875838, 40391, '<td valign="top">Wow! Perfect capture. Lighting, focus, colours, set up are all brilliant! More than half way through and my first 10 and Fav. Thank you.</td>', 'Wow! Perfect capture. Lighting, focus, colours, set up are all brilliant! More than half way through and my first 10 and Fav. Thank you.', '2010-05-06 05:30:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993900, 875646, 40391, '<td valign="top">Great focus, D0F, lighting and contrast. 9.</td>', 'Great focus, D0F, lighting and contrast. 9.', '2010-05-06 05:33:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993903, 875369, 40391, '<td valign="top">I love the tone, focus and location. Well done 9.</td>', 'I love the tone, focus and location. Well done 9.', '2010-05-06 05:34:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993907, 875492, 40391, '<td valign="top">I''d say it''s to the other side ;-)<br/> <br/>Great location. Perhaps this could have been even better from a lower perspective? 6</td>', 'I''d say it''s to the other side ;-) Great location. Perhaps this could have been even better from a lower perspective? 6', '2010-05-06 05:36:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993917, 872690, 40391, '<td valign="top">Great capture of the lightning but the exposure was a little too long to maintian the focus of the plume for me. Perhaps a tighter crop on the lightning may have made improved the photo? 5</td>', 'Great capture of the lightning but the exposure was a little too long to maintian the focus of the plume for me. Perhaps a tighter crop on the lightning may have made improved the photo? 5', '2010-05-06 05:39:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993919, 875320, 40391, '<td valign="top">Happy Birthday Zoie!<br/> <br/>Nice shot. I would have prefered more of the sharpness of the focus on the eyes but well captured. 5</td>', 'Happy Birthday Zoie! Nice shot. I would have prefered more of the sharpness of the focus on the eyes but well captured. 5', '2010-05-06 05:42:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993922, 875938, 74166, '<td valign="top">Nicely captured</td>', 'Nicely captured', '2010-05-06 05:44:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993924, 875631, 40391, '<td valign="top">Great DoF! I would have cropped the top (fore) part of the bridge that''s slightly out of focus as I don''t feel it adds to this lovely shot. 7</td>', 'Great DoF! I would have cropped the top (fore) part of the bridge that''s slightly out of focus as I don''t feel it adds to this lovely shot. 7', '2010-05-06 05:47:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993925, 875471, 74166, '<td valign="top">Interesting subjects</td>', 'Interesting subjects', '2010-05-06 05:47:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993928, 875787, 74166, '<td valign="top">Great colors, nice perspective</td>', 'Great colors, nice perspective', '2010-05-06 05:47:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993930, 875988, 40391, '<td valign="top">Love the eyes and exposure. 8</td>', 'Love the eyes and exposure. 8', '2010-05-06 05:50:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993932, 875435, 40391, '<td valign="top">Nicely done! 8</td>', 'Nicely done! 8', '2010-05-06 05:51:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993933, 875812, 40391, '<td valign="top">Not a fan of the processing - sorry (especially around the pants, shoes and top of the bus) 3</td>', 'Not a fan of the processing - sorry (especially around the pants, shoes and top of the bus) 3', '2010-05-06 05:53:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993935, 876049, 40391, '<td valign="top">... of field - nice. 6</td>', '... of field - nice. 6', '2010-05-06 05:54:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993939, 874966, 40391, '<td valign="top">Nice colours but the lack of focus lets this shot down. 3</td>', 'Nice colours but the lack of focus lets this shot down. 3', '2010-05-06 05:59:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993960, 875838, 86218, '<td valign="top">Hope to see soem info on the PP here. Lovely image</td>', 'Hope to see soem info on the PP here. Lovely image', '2010-05-06 06:26:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993966, 864748, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: What an unusual photograph to offer, that''s interesting because the tray of sunglasses isn''t that unusual but the capture of it and presentation is unexpected. I like the way way the catchlight reflections themselves reflect a suggestion of sunshine. I also like how you have kept the number of sunglasses ambiguous.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Once we get past the novelty of the presentation, we are forced to consider the intrinsic interest level of the scene. This is quite low.<br/> <br/>Overall: An interesting choice and an interesting POV but I''m not sure that is enough to carry the day as a photographic work.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: What an unusual photograph to offer, that''s interesting because the tray of sunglasses isn''t that unusual but the capture of it and presentation is unexpected. I like the way way the catchlight reflections themselves reflect a suggestion of sunshine. I also like how you have kept the number of sunglasses ambiguous. Critical stuff: Once we get past the novelty of the presentation, we are forced to consider the intrinsic interest level of the scene. This is quite low. Overall: An interesting choice and an interesting POV but I''m not sure that is enough to carry the day as a photographic work.', '2010-05-06 06:42:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993970, 875435, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives:  This is a really impressive, high impact image. The star trails are superbly captured but the HDR handling of the scene and presentation of the vehicles is astonishing. One of those photos that I find humbling. I am sooooooo far off having the skills to be able to pull off a shot like this; it is just so well finished. In terms of narrative, it connects the every day to the big wide world and to the wider universe - quite a feat.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing<br/> <br/>Overall: Beautiful and awe inspiring. Stunning. 10 and a fav.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives:  This is a really impressive, high impact image. The star trails are superbly captured but the HDR handling of the scene and presentation of the vehicles is astonishing. One of those photos that I find humbling. I am sooooooo far off having the skills to be able to pull off a shot like this; it is just so well finished. In terms of narrative, it connects the every day to the big wide world and to the wider universe - quite a feat. Critical stuff: Nothing Overall: Beautiful and awe inspiring. Stunning. 10 and a fav.', '2010-05-06 06:48:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993971, 865477, 100393, '<td valign="top">Great capture - super effective and highly sellable too.</td>', 'Great capture - super effective and highly sellable too.', '2010-05-06 06:51:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993973, 864825, 75618, '<td valign="top">One of the standouts for me in this free study, great reflections, literally and figuratively... Was this shot in Asia? I''m guessing Phils because those equipments look familiar. 9</td>', 'One of the standouts for me in this free study, great reflections, literally and figuratively... Was this shot in Asia? I''m guessing Phils because those equipments look familiar. 9', '2010-05-06 06:53:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993974, 875519, 75618, '<td valign="top">Great atmosphere created by the mist and split-toning. 8+1</td>', 'Great atmosphere created by the mist and split-toning. 8+1', '2010-05-06 06:54:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993977, 875635, 75618, '<td valign="top">Love the PP, especially the limited color palette. It gives the image an otherworldly feel. 9</td>', 'Love the PP, especially the limited color palette. It gives the image an otherworldly feel. 9', '2010-05-06 06:55:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993988, 876103, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I really like these sorts of images where form and movement win out over detail and conventional representation. There is just the right amount of form here to communicate your subject and the amount of motion blur conveys a great sense of dynamism. I also really like the structursnon the right of the image, they give the impression of pending destination and ground the rider into an environmental context.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing<br/> <br/>Overall: Very compelling work. I like it a lot.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I really like these sorts of images where form and movement win out over detail and conventional representation. There is just the right amount of form here to communicate your subject and the amount of motion blur conveys a great sense of dynamism. I also really like the structursnon the right of the image, they give the impression of pending destination and ground the rider into an environmental context. Critical stuff: Nothing Overall: Very compelling work. I like it a lot.', '2010-05-06 07:03:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993990, 875838, 100393, '<td valign="top">Another fantastically well done star trail image, once again this image humbles me as a photographer - this is well off the scale of what I could achieve and it makes me sit up and take notice. Stunning clarity, amazing DOF, perfect coloration, lovely composition. I think this will have very wide appeal too - my bet for the blue.</td>', 'Another fantastically well done star trail image, once again this image humbles me as a photographer - this is well off the scale of what I could achieve and it makes me sit up and take notice. Stunning clarity, amazing DOF, perfect coloration, lovely composition. I think this will have very wide appeal too - my bet for the blue.', '2010-05-06 07:08:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993991, 876103, 75618, '<td valign="top">WOW! Initially gave you a 7 but I''m giving you (a very biased) 10 upon second viewing. Evokes nostalgia, pleasant memories... =)</td>', 'WOW! Initially gave you a 7 but I''m giving you (a very biased) 10 upon second viewing. Evokes nostalgia, pleasant memories... =)', '2010-05-06 07:09:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993995, 875129, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I like the narrow scope of this image; you have found a small piece of our world and made it the subject of your image - the inclusion of some background scenery emphasizes how tiny a part of our world this is and the car becomes more significant as a result. I think the coloration / toning works well to.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Sharpness. I think this is too soft to be truly effective, the brain gets bothered by it and ceases to be interested in your scene.<br/> <br/>Overall: Conceptually strong but with some technical deficits.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I like the narrow scope of this image; you have found a small piece of our world and made it the subject of your image - the inclusion of some background scenery emphasizes how tiny a part of our world this is and the car becomes more significant as a result. I think the coloration / toning works well to. Critical stuff: Sharpness. I think this is too soft to be truly effective, the brain gets bothered by it and ceases to be interested in your scene. Overall: Conceptually strong but with some technical deficits.', '2010-05-06 07:13:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5993998, 875917, 75618, '<td valign="top">This is a great study of contrasts... the water and sky, man-made and natural. Good job on the unconventional comp and PP. 9</td>', 'This is a great study of contrasts... the water and sky, man-made and natural. Good job on the unconventional comp and PP. 9', '2010-05-06 07:15:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(5994002, 875905, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I like unconventional portraits and this one is no different in that regard. The partial face works really well, the nailed eye focus and the expression hold our interest really well. I love the background too, especially the coloration of the scene - it reminds me of Nik software''s ''ink'' filter in Color Efex Pro; one of my favourites.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing<br/> <br/>Overall: A very effective image benefitting from a great and brave choice of composition.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I like unconventional portraits and this one is no different in that regard. The partial face works really well, the nailed eye focus and the expression hold our interest really well. I love the background too, especially the coloration of the scene - it reminds me of Nik software''s ''ink'' filter in Color Efex Pro; one of my favourites. Critical stuff: Nothing Overall: A very effective image benefitting from a great and brave choice of composition.', '2010-05-06 07:21:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5994006, 873282, 64086, '<td valign="top">I really like this composition, the color and the texture. My only minor suggestion is that I would try processing the water differently. there''s some distracting smudges that take my eye away from the boats, perhaps from noise reduction? Great photo.</td>', 'I really like this composition, the color and the texture. My only minor suggestion is that I would try processing the water differently. there''s some distracting smudges that take my eye away from the boats, perhaps from noise reduction? Great photo.', '2010-05-06 07:24:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5994009, 875640, 64086, '<td valign="top">Great photo and the processing really adds nicely to the mood.</td>', 'Great photo and the processing really adds nicely to the mood.', '2010-05-06 07:27:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5994010, 876100, 100393, '<td valign="top">You have the measure of this scene, the clouds are the star and you have composed the frame perfectly, with exactly the optimal mix of sea, city and sky.<br/> <br/>The contrast handling in the cloud area is just flat out brilliant and the sense of darkness at the left of the image really is ominous.<br/> <br/>I think I know who''s image this is but that''s not going to stop me giving a score - great work.</td>', 'You have the measure of this scene, the clouds are the star and you have composed the frame perfectly, with exactly the optimal mix of sea, city and sky. The contrast handling in the cloud area is just flat out brilliant and the sense of darkness at the left of the image really is ominous. I think I know who''s image this is but that''s not going to stop me giving a score - great work.', '2010-05-06 07:27:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5994013, 875936, 64086, '<td valign="top">I like teh side view. The pose of the hand adds a feeling of frustration for me, while her facial expression seems more contemplative. Perhaps that is your intention but my eye keeps being drawn to the hand. I like the contrast, but the face and left shoulder have lost some detail on my screen. Nice photo.</td>', 'I like teh side view. The pose of the hand adds a feeling of frustration for me, while her facial expression seems more contemplative. Perhaps that is your intention but my eye keeps being drawn to the hand. I like the contrast, but the face and left shoulder have lost some detail on my screen. Nice photo.', '2010-05-06 07:35:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5994062, 872000, 7889, '<td valign="top">My absolute favourite in this challenge and my top vote. I think this would make a wonderful print to hang.</td>', 'My absolute favourite in this challenge and my top vote. I think this would make a wonderful print to hang.', '2010-05-06 08:47:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(5994063, 874353, 7889, '<td valign="top">This is such a wonderful photograph. Hope it does well for you</td>', 'This is such a wonderful photograph. Hope it does well for you', '2010-05-06 08:48:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5994065, 876103, 7889, '<td valign="top">One of my top votes in this challenge though I doubt that it is appealing to the majority on here, hope I am wrong and this finishes high.</td>', 'One of my top votes in this challenge though I doubt that it is appealing to the majority on here, hope I am wrong and this finishes high.', '2010-05-06 08:49:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(5994066, 867395, 7889, '<td valign="top">Such a lovely photo and b&amp;w works so well here. One of my top vots. Good luck.</td>', 'Such a lovely photo and b&w works so well here. One of my top vots. Good luck.', '2010-05-06 08:49:53.000000', NULL, 1),
