(5995570, 876064, 63218, '<td valign="top">This is the most intense red color I think I''ve ever seen, or tried to photograph. The colors are so hot they look fake, even in real life.  Looks to me like your reds are a little bit clipped (so were mine). I get pretty good results metering on the green leaves. Anyway, a 10 from me for the sheer operatic bravura.</td>', 'This is the most intense red color I think I''ve ever seen, or tried to photograph. The colors are so hot they look fake, even in real life.  Looks to me like your reds are a little bit clipped (so were mine). I get pretty good results metering on the green leaves. Anyway, a 10 from me for the sheer operatic bravura.', '2010-05-07 12:04:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5995600, 873434, 77543, '<td valign="top">It''s strange how the reflection of the sky is a different colour from the sky :-)</td>', 'It''s strange how the reflection of the sky is a different colour from the sky :-)', '2010-05-07 12:39:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(5995615, 866800, 63218, '<td valign="top">The tulip makes a beautiful, soft theatre for these tiny martially striped bugs. This is perfectly done. Reminds me irresistibly of a fine pencil drawing.  I like it especially for the view of life I could never get without a camera lens. 10.</td>', 'The tulip makes a beautiful, soft theatre for these tiny martially striped bugs. This is perfectly done. Reminds me irresistibly of a fine pencil drawing.  I like it especially for the view of life I could never get without a camera lens. 10.', '2010-05-07 12:54:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(5995633, 864633, 63218, '<td valign="top">The contrast between the filled-with-light petals (they look made of glass) and the earthy reality of the bee &amp; FG petals holds my interest.  I like looking at it. The negative space is filled with energy &amp; depth that complements the subject. Maybe the best shot of a Bird of Paradise flower, ever. 10</td>', 'The contrast between the filled-with-light petals (they look made of glass) and the earthy reality of the bee & FG petals holds my interest.  I like looking at it. The negative space is filled with energy & depth that complements the subject. Maybe the best shot of a Bird of Paradise flower, ever. 10', '2010-05-07 13:02:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(5995644, 875984, 104841, '<td valign="top">I normally don''t like pet photos but I don''t mind this one.  The reason I do like this one is it appears that you have set up the shot (composition as well) and I like the contrast of the oranges and the green eyes.</td>', 'I normally don''t like pet photos but I don''t mind this one.  The reason I do like this one is it appears that you have set up the shot (composition as well) and I like the contrast of the oranges and the green eyes.', '2010-05-07 13:05:25.000000', NULL, 1),
