(5997262, 876116, 88850, '<td valign="top">Nice score, Penny.  I like the textures and the reflection is great.</td>', 'Nice score, Penny.  I like the textures and the reflection is great.', '2010-05-08 14:07:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(5997263, 872000, 4482, '<td valign="top">Magnifique!</td>', 'Magnifique!', '2010-05-08 14:07:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5997268, 867926, 88850, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Lev!  Great finish for a great photo.</td>', 'Congratulations Lev!  Great finish for a great photo.', '2010-05-08 14:11:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(5997280, 872056, 5112, '<td valign="top">The bokeh is alright, except for that one out of focus stick to the left of the bird (and the bird seems to be looking at it - it isn''t but the direction of the eyes lead you to that OOF post).  I think the background loses effectiveness to the top, where you have the OOF grasses - it''s like you''re including too much extraneous information.  I wish there was a little more at the bottom of the image, possibly a little less at top, and also possibly that the bird would be more towards the right hand side of the frame looking into it, rather than in the middle at bottom.<br/> <br/>The light looks to be a tad harsh.  Both the bird and the fence are a tad too contrasty at top.  The flowers in the background also look a bit too bright to make a truly soft bokeh (notice all the yellow outlines).<br/> <br/>In other words, a lot of potential, but possibly a bit better light and more careful composition would improve a photo like this quite a bit.<br/> <br/>I do hope this helps.</td>', 'The bokeh is alright, except for that one out of focus stick to the left of the bird (and the bird seems to be looking at it - it isn''t but the direction of the eyes lead you to that OOF post).  I think the background loses effectiveness to the top, where you have the OOF grasses - it''s like you''re including too much extraneous information.  I wish there was a little more at the bottom of the image, possibly a little less at top, and also possibly that the bird would be more towards the right hand side of the frame looking into it, rather than in the middle at bottom. The light looks to be a tad harsh.  Both the bird and the fence are a tad too contrasty at top.  The flowers in the background also look a bit too bright to make a truly soft bokeh (notice all the yellow outlines). In other words, a lot of potential, but possibly a bit better light and more careful composition would improve a photo like this quite a bit. I do hope this helps.', '2010-05-08 14:27:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(5997284, 874835, 87252, '<td valign="top">Wow, great great shot Paul.</td>', 'Wow, great great shot Paul.', '2010-05-08 14:30:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5997292, 875565, 93714, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Tammster:</b></div><hr/><i> Very interesting whatever kind of bird this is. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually that''s a good question; I have no idea.  I was in the San Diego zoo aviary chasing him around for a while before he posed long enough to get the shot.  He is pretty unusual, sort of between a parrot and huge black bird.  Thank you for your vote and comment, it is much appreciated.<br/>Frank</td>', 'Originally posted by Tammster: Very interesting whatever kind of bird this is.   Actually that''s a good question; I have no idea.  I was in the San Diego zoo aviary chasing him around for a while before he posed long enough to get the shot.  He is pretty unusual, sort of between a parrot and huge black bird.  Thank you for your vote and comment, it is much appreciated.Frank', '2010-05-08 14:34:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5997294, 872056, 114225, '<td valign="top">I like the photo overall. I did feel the bird was a bit overpowered by the background, and also a bit too centered. Maybe crop it a bit to have slightly less background above the bird, and a little less of the right side of the photo (so it looks like the bird is looking into the empty space.<br/> <br/>Edit: I didn''t read ursula''s comment before I posted mine, I swear! Glad to know I''m thinking along the same lines as one of the greats :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-05-08 13:38:22.</i></td>', 'I like the photo overall. I did feel the bird was a bit overpowered by the background, and also a bit too centered. Maybe crop it a bit to have slightly less background above the bird, and a little less of the right side of the photo (so it looks like the bird is looking into the empty space. Edit: I didn''t read ursula''s comment before I posted mine, I swear! Glad to know I''m thinking along the same lines as one of the greats :)', '2010-05-08 14:37:01.000000', '2010-05-08 14:38:22.000000', 0),
(5997295, 867395, 47378, '<td valign="top">When I first looked at this, I thought "there must be a cloned-out wire holding her up". I guess I was wrong! :) This is one of the best pictures I''ve ever seen here on DPC, and the fact that she can pose like that is amazing! First class job by photographer and model!</td>', 'When I first looked at this, I thought "there must be a cloned-out wire holding her up". I guess I was wrong! :) This is one of the best pictures I''ve ever seen here on DPC, and the fact that she can pose like that is amazing! First class job by photographer and model!', '2010-05-08 14:37:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(5997298, 875253, 62895, '<td valign="top">This is amazing. You''ve captured a tremendous sense of atmosphere.</td>', 'This is amazing. You''ve captured a tremendous sense of atmosphere.', '2010-05-08 14:38:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(5997308, 867395, 19936, '<td valign="top">Although just looking at this photo makes my toes hurt it is, of course, another brilliant shot by Jennifer.  Congratulations on a blue in a Free Study!</td>', 'Although just looking at this photo makes my toes hurt it is, of course, another brilliant shot by Jennifer.  Congratulations on a blue in a Free Study!', '2010-05-08 14:42:32.000000', NULL, 0),
