(5997953, 864633, 35560, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pixelpig:</b></div><hr/><i> The contrast between the filled-with-light petals (they look made of glass) and the earthy reality of the bee &amp; FG petals holds my interest.  I like looking at it. The negative space is filled with energy &amp; depth that complements the subject. Maybe the best shot of a Bird of Paradise flower, ever. 10 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank your for your informative comment and vote.</td>', 'Originally posted by pixelpig: The contrast between the filled-with-light petals (they look made of glass) and the earthy reality of the bee & FG petals holds my interest.  I like looking at it. The negative space is filled with energy & depth that complements the subject. Maybe the best shot of a Bird of Paradise flower, ever. 10   Thank your for your informative comment and vote.', '2010-05-09 02:00:38.000000', NULL, 0),
