(6015755, 876125, 113419, '<td valign="top">I can''t really give any suggestions here as I gave it a 9.  I have read through what others have written and what I see mostly is folks think it''s overprocessed.  So that explains some things for me....folks here don''t like overprocessed; but I do and I have to be really careful when I''m preparing photos as entries here cause I tend to overprocess.  What I do is process a photo two ways....the way I like it; then go back and do one that I think is acceptable for DPC.  Then I enter what I like and as true to form if I enter what I like I get blasted.  And usually they are right so that has helped me alot.<br/>Although for this pic, I really don''t see what they are talking about as this photo looks very true to me, I''ve walked into lots of fields to catch lots of horses at many different times of day and I think this is an excellent shot.</td>', 'I can''t really give any suggestions here as I gave it a 9.  I have read through what others have written and what I see mostly is folks think it''s overprocessed.  So that explains some things for me....folks here don''t like overprocessed; but I do and I have to be really careful when I''m preparing photos as entries here cause I tend to overprocess.  What I do is process a photo two ways....the way I like it; then go back and do one that I think is acceptable for DPC.  Then I enter what I like and as true to form if I enter what I like I get blasted.  And usually they are right so that has helped me alot.Although for this pic, I really don''t see what they are talking about as this photo looks very true to me, I''ve walked into lots of fields to catch lots of horses at many different times of day and I think this is an excellent shot.', '2010-05-19 10:55:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(6017201, 867890, 103142, '<td valign="top">I completely disagree with the previous comment -- the people add interest and a sense of scale. Much, much better with the people! :)</td>', 'I completely disagree with the previous comment -- the people add interest and a sense of scale. Much, much better with the people! :)', '2010-05-19 20:53:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(6017220, 867890, 112828, '<td valign="top">Other than the people, I would have given this a 4..  As it was you got a six.. And yes, I can <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=jump&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1003072&amp;FORUM_POST_ID=6017176" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">understand the 1 vote</a>.  This was a very difficult scene, but would have been much better a bit later.  The sky needed to equalize in brightness with the ground.  Obviously a HDR would have been ideal.  As a result your sky is blown out and the ground is dark, unsaturated, and noisy.  I really shouldn''t have voted 6 here, but I liked the people very much.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-05-19 19:59:50.</i></td>', 'Other than the people, I would have given this a 4..  As it was you got a six.. And yes, I can understand the 1 vote.  This was a very difficult scene, but would have been much better a bit later.  The sky needed to equalize in brightness with the ground.  Obviously a HDR would have been ideal.  As a result your sky is blown out and the ground is dark, unsaturated, and noisy.  I really shouldn''t have voted 6 here, but I liked the people very much.', '2010-05-19 20:59:07.000000', '2010-05-19 20:59:50.000000', 0),
